I have successfully resolved the issue where active environments/configurations without a consumer Code Assist tier surface generic, confusing error messages when the `/privacy` workflow is invoked. 

Here is a summary of the implementation:

1. **Created Custom Tier Error** ([usePrivacySettings.ts](file:///usr/local/google/home/joneba/ssr-prototype/gcli-intern-project/tools/caretaker-agent/evals/pr-generation/run_outputs/medium_golden_3.5_flash/agent_environments/gemini_cli_2407/tmp/pr/gemini-cli/packages/cli/src/ui/hooks/usePrivacySettings.ts)):
   - Declared a custom class `TierUnavailableError` extending `Error`.
   - Updated helper `getCodeAssistServerOrFail(config)` to throw `TierUnavailableError` on missing OAuth session context or undefined project IDs.
   - Introduced `isTierUnavailableError` matching instances of `TierUnavailableError` or errors matching `/does not have a current tier/i`.

2. **Handled Tier Unavailable States Safely & Gracefully** ([usePrivacySettings.ts](file:///usr/local/google/home/joneba/ssr-prototype/gcli-intern-project/tools/caretaker-agent/evals/pr-generation/run_outputs/medium_golden_3.5_flash/agent_environments/gemini_cli_2407/tmp/pr/gemini-cli/packages/cli/src/ui/hooks/usePrivacySettings.ts)):
   - Added an `isTierUnavailable` boolean property to the `PrivacyState` interface.
   - Checked if `server.userTier` is undefined, setting `isTierUnavailable` to true and returning early without error strings.
   - Intercepted consumer tier failures in the loading/updating `catch` blocks using the new `isTierUnavailableError` helper to gracefully suppress error popups.

3. **Informed Users and Guided Next Steps** ([CloudFreePrivacyNotice.tsx](file:///usr/local/google/home/joneba/ssr-prototype/gcli-intern-project/tools/caretaker-agent/evals/pr-generation/run_outputs/medium_golden_3.5_flash/agent_environments/gemini_cli_2407/tmp/pr/gemini-cli/packages/cli/src/ui/privacy/CloudFreePrivacyNotice.tsx)):
   - Rendered a custom, highly informative notification notice when `isTierUnavailable` is true. The UI instructs the user that opt-in settings are inapplicable, references enterprise/Workspace accounts, guides them to specify the `GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT` environment variable, links to the official documentation, and directs them to exit by pressing `Esc`.
   - Updated the `keypress` listener block to handle `isTierUnavailable` and cleanly trigger `onExit` when the Escape key is clicked.

4. **Added Comprehensive Unit Tests**:
   - Modified and created new test cases in [usePrivacySettings.test.tsx](file:///usr/local/google/home/joneba/ssr-prototype/gcli-intern-project/tools/caretaker-agent/evals/pr-generation/run_outputs/medium_golden_3.5_flash/agent_environments/gemini_cli_2407/tmp/pr/gemini-cli/packages/cli/src/ui/hooks/usePrivacySettings.test.tsx) and [CloudFreePrivacyNotice.test.tsx](file:///usr/local/google/home/joneba/ssr-prototype/gcli-intern-project/tools/caretaker-agent/evals/pr-generation/run_outputs/medium_golden_3.5_flash/agent_environments/gemini_cli_2407/tmp/pr/gemini-cli/packages/cli/src/ui/privacy/CloudFreePrivacyNotice.test.tsx) spanning all 5 requested verification scenarios. All unit tests ran under the correct environment (Node 20) and passed flawlessly.
